<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Scott is a 41-year-old naval officer with stage 1 hypertension on lifestyle measures and nicotine dependence in early remission, who comes for a preventive visit about three months before his expedition sails. He has not smoked his pipe for seven weeks and still takes varenicline, now without nausea. His home blood pressure readings over the last week average about 134/84. He has cut his salt, eats fruit at lunch, and trains three times a week, walking with a weighted pack and running. He drinks a glass or two of wine with dinner on three evenings a week. His mood is good and he is sleeping six to seven hours. He wants his prevention up to date and his affairs settled before he leaves. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 41</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Home average about 134/84 on lifestyle measures</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No pipe for seven weeks; on varenicline</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One or two glasses of wine on three evenings a week</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him face to face by Dr. Harrow-Mbeki. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Very good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Under pressure from fundraising and the timetable, but coping and sleeping</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No pipe for seven weeks; cravings now brief and rare</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Within the low-risk limits</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Training three times a week with a weighted pack, plus daily walking</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Less salt and more fruit and vegetables; regular meals</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six to seven hours on most nights</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Married, one partner; no concerns</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at work</td><td>Office work now; heavy loads and cold exposure expected on the expedition</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Audiometry normal last month; reading glasses only</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

