    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan made. Tetanus booster and influenza vaccine given; HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening ordered; travel medicine appointment booked for the ports on the voyage. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year, or on his return.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Stage 1 hypertension on lifestyle measures (I10)</content>. Office 134/84; home average about 134/84, still above the target below 130/80 after seven weeks of lifestyle measures. [S]<list><item>Continue lifestyle measures and home readings; decide about medicine at the three-month visit, as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Nicotine dependence, pipe tobacco, in early remission (F17.290)</content>. No tobacco for seven weeks. [S]<list><item>Continue varenicline; no pipe or tobacco in his expedition kit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>134/84 mmHg; stage 1 hypertension on lifestyle measures</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0; PHQ-9 3 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>GAD-7 4 at intake; repeat before departure</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco cessation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Abstinent for seven weeks on varenicline; relapse prevention for months of isolation discussed</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 3 at intake, below the threshold for men</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Begins at 45 for adults at average risk; no family history known to him</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time antibody test for adults 18 to 79, drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time triple panel drawn today; vaccination to follow if he is not immune</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.3% and fasting glucose 92 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL cholesterol 122 mg/dL at intake; ten-year risk low; no statin indicated</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap given today; no dose recorded in the last ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today before months in a shared hut</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Declined</td><td>Discussed; he chose not to have it now</td></tr><tr><td>Measles, mumps, and rubella</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two documented doses in childhood</td></tr><tr><td>Travel vaccines and advice</td><td>Referred</td><td>Travel medicine clinic for the ports on the voyage south, including hepatitis A and typhoid vaccines as indicated</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer counseling and dental care</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sun and snow-glare protection, with glacier glasses, discussed; dental examination and cleaning done last month</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine; Influenza vaccine, current season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: 2025 AHA/ACC/AANP/AAPA/ABC/ACCP/ACPM/AGS/AMA/ASPC/NMA/PCNA/SGIM Guideline for the Prevention, Detection, Evaluation and Management of High Blood Pressure in Adults (Jones DW, et al. Circulation 2025;152(11):e114-e218) (2025); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, hypertension monograph (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Three-month review in six weeks with home blood pressure readings. Screening results through the patient portal. Travel medicine this month. Next scheduled visit 1910-04-21: three-month review: blood pressure above target, starting losartan, and cold-injury and first aid training. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent, because he will be months beyond reach of a hospital and, for much of the year, of any evacuation. He named a health care agent and a second agent, and a health care proxy form was completed; both are recorded in the chart and are not named here. He wants full treatment, including resuscitation, if he is ill or injured, with treatment in the field first and evacuation when it is possible. He asked that a copy travel with his medical summary in the expedition&apos;s medical kit. The plan will be revisited on his return or after any serious illness. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
